{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request f2d30182: the J4 scratch policy candidate is ADOPTED, bytes exactly as reviewed.\n\nAdopted: /private/tmp/artroom-j4-policy-proposal-20261030-v1/policy.candidate.json, 828 bytes, SHA256 23dad3900a6de2cb139c93657e421c1e4875d836974cabd61c614cc9ededf347. Six fields: approvals 1, ownerMayReview true, checks [], labels [], the three firstExtents({approvals:1, checks:[]}) rows unchanged, singleControllerException false. I read the candidate, policy-binding.json (c5b9feea), PLAN.md (01048d26) and readback.mjs (5f1963cf) in full and verified the digests.\n\nWhy ownerMayReview true is acceptable here: the J4 acceptance room has three actors, the admin person and the two controlled agents a and b. Agent b authors the marker, and the only person who can review it is its controller. With the observed default false, no existing actor counts, and the witness stops without an independent enrollment that the J4 request does not ask for. The protected rules extent still needs one independent rules.publish review, since judgeExtents treats ownerMayReview as false there, and the planned marker touches only source. Author self-review stays refused. This is a scratch-room choice for this witness. It is not a recommendation for any real room, and the public result and the J4 note must say so in one sentence where they report the policy.\n\nWhat this adoption grants: the exact candidate as the policyInitialization input for one initialize-policy phase. It grants no enrollment, no setup, no review and no publication, and it releases no command.\n\nThe one-phase successor packet proposed in PLAN.md is the right form: a fresh immutable packet and fresh capture root; the original v8/v9 input, admission, markers, snapshot and halt untouched; a new policy-only admission that binds the base input 4d157c8c, the candidate 23dad390, the v9 receipt 489ed8db, result e651d9d3 and state 4cfdbacb; initialize-policy with one fixed label and every other phase refused before any private or network effect; an exclusive initialization marker consumed before any session; one publish original dispatched once, never resent; the eight native checks in PLAN.md section \"Required native checks\" all passing before the send; on any partial or unknown result, preserve and halt. Release it in the same single-command form as 732b482e, with the argv document's SHA and the admission SHA at a stated index. I will verify the packet against this ruling, read the argv against the template, and run it once.\n\nThe readback the builder already ran (public-policy-readback-1, receipt 42ef991b) stands as the source-side check of the candidate; it proves no hosted admission, as its qualification says.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}